			<div class="content" id="post-content-2156014">
									

<p>The fact that this is essentially people with Tear Sickness from Bioshock Infinite bugs me to no end.</p>
<p>For those of you who don't know, Tear Sickness (referred to on the Bioshock Wiki as being &quot;Merged&quot;) is what happens to some corpses in Infinite when Elizabeth enters a new universe/timeline via a tear. Living individuals often get nosebleeds as their memories try to compensate for the incongruity with the one they originated from. Dead individuals, however&#8230; well, it's somewhat inconsistent, but usually, if their corpse is in close proximity to an opened tear, they start phasing in and out of existence, have jerky movements, and talk in a distorted voice.</p>
<p>This, combined with the ability to move between alternate timelines the Foundation has, makes me see this as Bioshock Infinite: The SCP. And as much as I love Infinite, this concept doesn't feel original at all.</p>
<p>-1</p>

